<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert II de la Marck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1468–<a href="/years/1536">1536</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert II de la Marck was lord of Sedan and duke of Bouillon, known as the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-de-la-marck">Boar of the Ardennes</a>. He fortified Sedan and claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, owing allegiance to neither the French king nor the emperor. Switching between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, in 1521 he declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, provoking the first war between Charles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-duke-of-nevers">Francis I</a>, and lost Bouillon for a time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-ii-de-la-marck.jpg" alt="Robert II de la Marck" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author (French art) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Beauregard_-_Robert_II_de_La_Marck.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
